---
import SiteHeader from "../../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="UTF-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png" />
		<title>Pamir Trail — Olivia Fjord Sloth</title>
		<meta name="description" content="A practical account of hiking the Pamir Trail in Tajikistan, including route notes and lessons from the trail." />
	</head>

	<body>

		<SiteHeader />


		<main>
<!-- HERO -->

			<section class="hero">

				<p class="eyebrow">TAJIKISTAN · PAMIR TRAIL</p>

				<h1>Pamir Trail</h1>

				<p class="lead">
					I had planned to do this hike alone. Then I managed to convince
					my friend Mikkel to come with me, and I was very happy I did.
				</p>

				<p class="lead">
					The hike turned out to be a lot harder than I had imagined.
					We had to carry food for the whole route, our backpacks were
					ridiculously heavy, and we met almost no one along the way.
				</p>

				<p class="lead">
					But it was incredible. Probably the most beautiful hike I have
					ever done. Ever since, walking the full 1,313 km Pamir Trail has
					been very high on my list of things I want to do.
				</p>

			</section>


			<!-- QUICK INFO -->

			<section class="quick-info">

				<div>
					<p class="label">WHEN I HIKED IT</p>
					<p>July 2024</p>
				</div>

				<div>
					<p class="label">MY SECTION</p>
					<p>Fann Mountains</p>
				</div>

				<div>
					<p class="label">DISTANCE</p>
					<p>158.5 km</p>
				</div>

				<div>
					<p class="label">HIGHEST PASS</p>
					<p>4,750 m</p>
				</div>

			</section>


			<!-- THE TRAIL -->

			<section class="content-section">

				<p class="section-label">THE TRAIL</p>

				<div class="text">

					<p>
						The full Pamir Trail runs for 1,313 km through Tajikistan.
						We walked the first section through the Fann Mountains.
					</p>

					<p>
						It is still one of the most beautiful hikes I have ever done.
						We met almost no other tourists along the way, and the local
						people we met were incredibly kind.
					</p>

					<p>
						The route is not marked, but we found it quite easy to navigate
						using the GPX route.
					</p>

					<p>
						The Pamir Trail website is fantastic. We used it for planning,
						and you can find descriptions of the route and download the GPX
						files there.
					</p>

					<a
						class="external-link"
						href="https://www.pamirtrail.org/the-trail"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer"
					>
						Pamir Trail route and GPX files →
					</a>

				</div>

			</section>


			<!-- GETTING THERE -->

			<section class="content-section">

				<p class="section-label">GETTING THERE</p>

				<div class="text">

					<p>
						We flew to Samarkand in Uzbekistan and took a marshrutka
						from there towards the Tajik border.
					</p>

					<p>
						Crossing the border was easy. On the Tajik side, we took
						a shared taxi to Panjakent.
					</p>

				</div>

			</section>


			<!-- CAMPING GAS -->

			<section class="content-section">

				<p class="section-label">CAMPING GAS</p>

				<div class="text">

					<p>
						Camping gas was actually one of the things I was worried
						about before the trip. I found it surprisingly difficult
						to figure out from home where we would be able to buy it.
					</p>

					<p>
						We found camping gas at Salom Hostel in Panjakent.
						That was in July 2024, so I can’t promise they still sell it.
						I would give them a call before relying on it.
					</p>

				</div>

			</section>


			<!-- FOOD & WATER -->

			<section class="content-section">

				<p class="section-label">FOOD & WATER</p>

				<div class="text">

					<p>
						You need to plan your food properly. It was almost impossible
						to buy food along the section we walked, so we carried what
						we needed.
					</p>

					<p>
						Water was much easier. There were plenty of streams and water
						sources along the route. We used a water filter just in case.
					</p>

				</div>

			</section>


			<!-- WEATHER & SAFETY -->

			<section class="content-section">

				<p class="section-label">WEATHER & SAFETY</p>

				<div class="text">

					<p>
						This is a remote hike. We had long stretches without mobile
						reception, so I would bring a satellite communicator such as
						a Garmin inReach in case something goes wrong.
					</p>

					<p>
						The weather can change very quickly in the mountains.
						We had thunderstorms appear seemingly out of nowhere.
						I would not do this hike without being comfortable in the
						mountains and knowing how to react when the weather changes.
					</p>

				</div>

			</section>


			<!-- WOULD I GO BACK -->

			<section class="content-section final-section">

				<p class="section-label">WOULD I GO BACK?</p>

				<div class="text">

					<p class="big-text">
						Absolutely.
					</p>

					<p>
						The landscape is huge, wild and incredibly remote.
						Walking the entire Pamir Trail is still very high on my list
						of things I want to do.
					</p>

				</div>

			</section>

		</main>

		<SiteFooter />
	</body>
</html>


<style>

	/* GENERAL */

	* {
		box-sizing: border-box;
	}

	html,
	body {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		background: #f4f1ea;
		color: #171717;
	}

	body {
		font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
	}

	a {
		color: inherit;
		text-decoration: none;
	}


	/* HEADER */

	header {
		padding: 30px 48px;

		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		align-items: center;
	}

	.name {
		font-size: 22px;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
	}

	nav {
		display: flex;
		gap: 28px;
	}

	nav a {
		font-size: 15px;
	}

	nav .active {
		border-bottom: 1px solid #171717;
	}


	/* HERO */

	.hero {
		max-width: 1200px;
		margin: 100px auto 110px;
		padding: 0 48px;
	}

	.eyebrow,
	.section-label,
	.label {
		margin: 0 0 20px;

		font-size: 11px;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.18em;
	}

	.hero h1 {
		margin: 0;

		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: clamp(72px, 9vw, 130px);
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 0.92;
		letter-spacing: -0.04em;
	}
	.lead {
	max-width: 800px;
	margin: 22px 0 0;

	font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
	font-size: clamp(23px, 2.6vw, 34px);
	line-height: 1.45;

	color: #555;
}

	.hero h1 + .lead {
		margin-top: 45px;
	}


	/* QUICK INFO */

	.quick-info {
		max-width: 1200px;
		margin: 0 auto 120px;
		padding: 50px 48px;

		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
		gap: 40px;

		border-top: 1px solid #b9b3a9;
		border-bottom: 1px solid #b9b3a9;
	}

	.quick-info p:not(.label) {
		margin: 0;

		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: 21px;
		line-height: 1.4;
	}


	/* CONTENT */

	.content-section {
		max-width: 1000px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 0 48px 110px;
	}

	.text {
		max-width: 700px;
		margin-left: auto;
	}

	.text p {
		margin: 0 0 30px;

		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: 21px;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.external-link {
		display: inline-block;

		margin-top: 10px;
		padding-bottom: 4px;

		font-size: 14px;
		font-weight: 700;

		border-bottom: 1px solid #171717;
	}

	.big-text {
		font-size: 42px !important;
		line-height: 1.15 !important;
	}

	.final-section {
		padding-bottom: 150px;
	}


	/* MOBILE */

	@media (max-width: 800px) {

		header {
			padding: 24px 20px;
		}

		.name {
			font-size: 17px;
		}

		nav {
			gap: 12px;
		}

		nav a {
			font-size: 12px;
		}


		.hero {
			margin: 60px auto 80px;
			padding: 0 24px;
		}

		.hero h1 {
			font-size: 64px;
		}

		.lead {
			font-size: 22px;
		}


		.quick-info {
			margin-bottom: 90px;
			padding: 40px 24px;

			grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
			gap: 40px 25px;
		}


		.content-section {
			padding: 0 24px 80px;
		}

		.text {
			margin-left: 0;
		}

		.text p {
			font-size: 19px;
		}

		.big-text {
			font-size: 34px !important;
		}
	}

</style>
